<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#F3ECE1;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 10px;">Is Sandstone Stucco Co a stucco contractor?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">No. It is an advertising service paid by independent stucco contractors. The contractor who inspects your wall quotes you directly and holds the contract, and the site does no stucco work and offers no warranty. In Alberta, stucco is not a compulsory-certification trade, so it is worth asking any contractor what they hold.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 10px;">What should I check before I hire a stucco contractor?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Alberta.ca advises insisting on a written contract, getting written estimates from more than one business, and making sure the contractor and tradespeople have Workers' Compensation Board coverage. The City of Calgary says contractors need a valid City business licence, which you can confirm by calling 311. If a contractor sells in person away from their own premises and asks for money before the work is done, the Alberta prepaid contracting licence may apply, and Service Alberta has a licence search.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 10px;">Will you deal with my insurance company after hail damage?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">No. The site does not file, negotiate or manage claims, and it cannot say what an insurer will approve. IBC says hail damage is typically covered by home insurance, so check your own policy, and the City of Calgary advises contacting your insurer before you do repair work. A contractor can write a repair scope that you may give to your insurer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
